If the module "m" sends the message "a", the message "b" and the message "c" through the connection "k" to the process "p", the process "p" closes the connection "k".
If the module "m" writes the record "r" and the record "s" to the file "f", the module "n" reads the file "f".
If the state machine "sm" has the states "x" and "y", the module "m" launches the process "p".
The state machine "sm" starts in the state "x".
When the module "m" reads the value "rate" and the value "z", the module "m" does not change the value "z".
While the module "m" prints "a" and "b", the module "m" uses the module "n".
